  (subsection build
   (doc "How to build and test each component")
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
         Lisp interpreter (no services needed):
           cd lisp/ && dune build && dune runtest
           Tests are pure alcotest cases, no DB, no HTTP.

         Image (needs Postgres for full run, but builds
         without):
           cd image/ && dune build
           Run: dune exec bin/unikernel.ml (mirage/unix)
           Needs PG connection from env.

         Supervisor (needs Postgres for full run):
           cd supervisor/ && dune build
           Run: dune exec bin/supervisor.ml
           Needs PG connection, can boot images.

         Common:
           cd common/ && dune build && dune runtest

         Migrations:
           Applied by supervisor on boot, or manually via:
           psql -f migrations/NNN_xxx.sql

         Full dev boot:
           1. start Postgres
           2. dune exec supervisor/bin/supervisor.ml
              (supervisor runs migrations, then listens)
           3. ssh into a user's image
              (supervisor boots the image on connect)
   |))
   )
  )
  (subsection conventions
   (doc "Coding conventions for this project")
   (status partial)
   (details
    (doc (|
         v1 ADOPTED STACK (normative):
         - OCaml / dune (per poohstack); OCaml 5.x on the
           poohstack opam switch
         - Lwt for ALL unikernel I/O (supervisor, authd,
           image). Mirage's runtime is Lwt-based; the
           evaluator is Lwt-typed (eval returns value Lwt.t).
           Eio only for pure-unix dev tooling (e.g.
           lisp/bin/repl.ml), never inside unikernels.
         - pure-html (dream_html HTML core, no Dream) for
           HTML; use HTML.Hx.* not raw htmx attribute strings.
           txt ~raw:true for intentional raw-HTML injection.
         - httpaf-lwt-unix for image + supervisor + authd
           HTTP in v1. (There is no httpaf-mirage package on
           opam. Future Solo5 path: gluten-mirage + httpaf.)
         - Postgres via pgx_lwt + a custom Io_unix shim in v1
           (POSIX-flavored libs). pgx_lwt_mirage exists on the
           switch but needs a real Tcpip.Stack.V4V6 device,
           only available inside a true Mirage unikernel —
           that swap is a Solo5/v1.5 axis, not v1.
         - Auth via pricklypear's own authd unikernel (auth/),
           NOT wyo.auth. authd is the credential/token/audit
           trust boundary; supervisor calls it over internal
           HTTP RPC; images trust supervisor-asserted identity
           via the boot manifest.
         - SERIALIZABLE transactions by default for mutations
         - No ORM, no Postgres INHERITANCE, no premature
           abstraction; plain parameterized SQL
         - Additive-only schema migrations
         - The .borg file is the source of truth; if the
           implementation disagrees, the implementation is
           wrong — unless a plan pass rewrites the spec
         - Design changes go through borge plan/make/review;
           during make, file `borge issue new` instead of
           editing .borg

         DEFERRED CONVENTIONS (not v1-normative yet):
         - Solo5 target + Mirage-native transports
           (pgx_lwt_mirage, gluten-mirage, real VM boot)
         - mTLS/signed internal RPC between supervisor/authd
         - wyo.auth integration (explicitly not chosen for v1)
   |))
   )
  )
 )

)
